            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0079" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg67"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.24/150: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-02-27T22:00:00-04:00">February 27,
                            1943—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>323. Your 351, February 16, 9 a.m. Personal for the Minister from Wallace Murray.
                    I regret that the military authorities have <pb facs="0080" n="68" xml:id="pg68"
                    /> found it impossible to make available the two planes desired for the use of
                    Misr Air Lines. I am convinced, however, that the military authorities have gone
                    into the question very carefully but found it impossible to furnish the planes
                    at the present time because of the very urgent need of our Armed Forces for
                    planes of this type. [Murray.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
